jobs.description:
**REM Center Inc.**

Founded in 2021, REM CENTER Inc. is a non\-profit organization dedicated to the advancement of society through science, education and quality social services. We are a small team of community members, leaders, teachers, school leaders, friends and allies working together to contribute to the growth and health of our communities. We operate and support the Bronx HYPE Family Enrichment Center and the Haven Hope School\-Based Early Support Program in the Bronx.

The Haven and Hope School\-Based Early Support Program currently provides services to families and children in school districts 7, 11 and 12 in the Bronx. We provide families with case management, academic and social\-emotional supports, and concrete resources. We feel strongly about equity and access to high quality educational and social services, and we’re passionate about advocacy and community outreach.

**Mission**

We seek to understand community needs and contribute to the overall wellness, growth and development of society.

**Vision**

We are committed to creating access to quality social services, reducing economic inequality, and promoting sustainable practices in urban communities.

**Program Director Position**

The Program Director is primarily responsible for their site, including supervising staff, overseeing daily activities, and ensuring program goals are met and families are receiving quality services, building strong relationships with school leaders in the Bronx, and attending agency meetings and events. This role is ideal for someone who is extremely passionate about equity and access to high quality educational and social services. This position requires a commitment to trauma\-informed care and evidence\-based practices. The Program Director will report directly to the Associate Vice President.

Title: Director, School\-Based Early Supports

Work Location: 1250 Waters Place, Bronx, NY 10461

Work Hours: 9:00am\-5:00pm; Full\-Time/Exempt; evening and weekend work may be required.

Specific responsibilities include but are not limited to:

* Implements and maintains new preventive program in the East Bronx;
* Manages and oversees all aspects of their site;
* Ensures current knowledge of the ACS Prevention Standards, and implement the standards in all aspects of programming;
* Hires and recruit staff;
* Supervises, coach and supports all staff;
* Manages daily program operations;
* Creates a positive work culture and inclusive environment;
* Coaches and develops program supervisors and program support staff;
* Supervises case planners, case aides, and additional staff members as assigned;
* Ensures services are provided at a high quality level;
* Provides direct casework as needed;
* Completes home visits, and family and group counseling as needed;
* Implements research\-based programs and practices, including Triple P and Motivational Interviewing (MI);
* Listens to, empathizes, and connects with families;
* Carries oneself with the highest level of professionalism;
* Builds and maintains a collaborative partnership with school leaders; district leaders and community leaders;
* Attends agency and community organization events in districts 7, 11 and 12, community board meetings, and other meetings related to ACS, DYCD, and DOE;
* Represents the organization at external meetings, tabling events, and community events;
* Ensures program goals and objectives are met;
* Ensures timely submission of all required reports, including developing reports, FASPs, Connections and PROMIS;
* Maintains the general appearance of their work area and collaborates with staff to ensure high standards of cleanliness, organization and beauty of the physical work environment;
* Maintains flexibility, adaptability and poise at all times;
* Responds to emergencies outside of work hours;
* Performs other duties as assigned.

Minimum Qualifications

* Master's Degree in Social Work; Master’s in a related Human Services' accepted on a case by case basis;
* LMSW/LCSW (preferred);
* At least 3 years of supervisory experience;
* At least 5 years of administrative experience at a CBO or human services organization;
* Experience working directly with families, children and in a public school environment;
* Knowledge of ACS Prevention Standards and Policies, CONNECTIONS and PROMIS data systems;
* Excellent oral and written communication skills;
* Excellent time management and organization skills;
* Excellent interpersonal skills;
* The ability to travel within the South Bronx;
* The ability to lift up to 50lbs;
* The ability to remain calm and flexible under stressful or challenging situations;
* Available to work weekends and evenings as needed.

Preferred Qualifications

* Bilingual (Spanish and English);
* At least four (4\) years of experience living and/or working in the Bronx;
* Experience working in NYC Public Schools.

Full\-Time Employee Benefits:

* Healthcare Plan (Medical, Dental and Vision Insurance)
* Flexible Spending Account
* Life Insurance
* 401(k) \- 3% employer contribution
* Paid Time Off

REM Center Inc. is committed to a diverse workforce, and we seek diversity among applicants for this position. People of color, women, gay/lesbian/bisexual/transgender people, people with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply.

REM Center Inc. is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: $80,000\.00 \- $85,000\.00 per year

Benefits:

* 401(k)
* 401(k) matching
* Dental insurance
* Flexible spending account
* Health insurance
* Health savings account
* Life insurance
* Paid time off
* Vision insurance

Education:

* Master's (Required)

Experience:

* Preventive Experience/ACS Program Management: 2 years (Required)
* Social work: 1 year (Required)
* PROMIS and CNNX: 2 years (Preferred)
* Supervisory: 2 years (Required)

License/Certification:

* Social Work License (Preferred)

Work Location: In person
